{"assets":["/statement-assets/0f7fc6d25dadb7623f0acdf3fca618db45ab1f697010d97a1e083be6349b9958.png"],"contentKind":"statement","contestId":"346","diagnostics":[],"document":{"children":[{"attrs":{"level":1,"role":"title"},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"E. Doodle Jump"}],"kind":"heading"},{"attrs":{"role":"time_limit"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"time limit per test"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"2 seconds"}],"kind":"container"},{"attrs":{"role":"memory_limit"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"memory limit per test"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"256 megabytes"}],"kind":"container"},{"attrs":{"role":"body"},"children":[{"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":" In Doodle Jump the aim is to guide a four-legged creature called \"The Doodler\" up a never-ending series of platforms without falling. — Wikipedia. "}],"kind":"container"}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"It is a very popular game and xiaodao likes it very much. One day when playing the game she wondered whether there exists a platform that the doodler couldn't reach due to the limits of its jumping ability. Consider the following problem."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"There are "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"n"},{"kind":"text","text":" platforms. The height of the "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"x"},{"kind":"text","text":"-th ("},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"1 ≤ x ≤ n"},{"kind":"text","text":") platform is "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"a·x"},{"kind":"text","text":" mod "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"p"},{"kind":"text","text":", where "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"a"},{"kind":"text","text":" and "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"p"},{"kind":"text","text":" are positive co-prime integers. The maximum possible height of a Doodler's jump is "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"h"},{"kind":"text","text":". That is, it can jump from height "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"h1"},{"kind":"text","text":" to height "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"h2"},{"kind":"text","text":" ("},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"h1 < h2"},{"kind":"text","text":") if "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"h2 - h1 ≤ h"},{"kind":"text","text":". Initially, the Doodler is on the ground, the height of which is 0. The question is whether it can reach the highest platform or not."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"For example, when "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"a = 7"},{"kind":"text","text":", "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"n = 4"},{"kind":"text","text":", "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"p = 12"},{"kind":"text","text":", "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"h = 2"},{"kind":"text","text":", the heights of the platforms are "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"7"},{"kind":"text","text":", "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"2"},{"kind":"text","text":", "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"9"},{"kind":"text","text":", "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"4"},{"kind":"text","text":" as in the picture below. With the first jump the Doodler can jump to the platform at height "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"2"},{"kind":"text","text":", with the second one the Doodler can jump to the platform at height "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"4"},{"kind":"text","text":", but then it can't jump to any of the higher platforms. So, it can't reach the highest platform."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"attrs":{"alt":"","src":"/statement-assets/0f7fc6d25dadb7623f0acdf3fca618db45ab1f697010d97a1e083be6349b9958.png"},"kind":"image"}],"kind":"container"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"User xiaodao thought about the problem for a long time but didn't solve it, so she asks you for help. Also, she has a lot of instances of the problem. Your task is solve all of these instances."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"input_specification"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Input"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"The first line contains an integer "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"t"},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"(1 ≤ t ≤ 104)"},{"kind":"text","text":" — the number of problem instances. Each of the next "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"t"},{"kind":"text","text":" lines contains four integers "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"a"},{"kind":"text","text":", "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"n"},{"kind":"text","text":", "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"p"},{"kind":"text","text":" and "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"h"},{"kind":"text","text":" ("},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"1 ≤ a ≤ 109"},{"kind":"text","text":", "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"1 ≤ n < p ≤ 109"},{"kind":"text","text":", "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"0 ≤ h ≤ 109"},{"kind":"text","text":"). It's guaranteed that "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"a"},{"kind":"text","text":" and "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"p"},{"kind":"text","text":" are co-prime."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"output_specification"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Output"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"For each problem instance, if the Doodler can reach the highest platform, output \""},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"YES"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"\", otherwise output \""},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"NO"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"\"."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"samples"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Examples"}],"kind":"heading"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample"},"children":[{"attrs":{"role":"sample_input"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Input"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"3\n7 4 12 2\n7 1 9 4\n7 4 12 3\n"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample_output"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Output"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"NO\nNO\nYES\n"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"document"},"index":"E","problemCode":"346E","schema":2,"sourceKind":"html","sourceUrl":"https://codeforces.com/contest/346/problem/E"}